## Description
* **Breaking change:** GraphQL type `Vendor` used in XCatalog replaced with core `CommonVendor`
  * Example query:
```graphql
query($storeId: String!, $currencyCode: String!, $cultureName: String, $productId: String!) {
  product(id: $productId, storeId: $storeId, currencyCode: $currencyCode, cultureName: $cultureName) {
    id
    name
    vendor {
      id
      name
    }
    variations {
      id
      name
      vendor {
        id
        name
      }
    }
  }
}
```
* Moved SEO info shared code to *.Core project.
  * Check backward-compatibility of SEO info loading for category & product queries
```graphql
query($storeId: String!, $currencyCode: String!, $cultureName: String, $productId: String!, $categoryId: String!) {
  product(id: $productId, storeId: $storeId, currencyCode: $currencyCode, cultureName: $cultureName) {
    id
    name
    seoInfo {
      id
      name
      semanticUrl
    }
    variations {
      id
      name      
      seoInfo {
        id
        name
        semanticUrl
      }
    }
  }
  category(id: $categoryId, storeId: $storeId, currencyCode: $currencyCode, cultureName: $cultureName) {
    id
    name
    seoInfo {
      id
      name
      semanticUrl
    }
  }
}
```
* Support of enums in filters
  * Fixes https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/PT-10387
```graphql
query($storeId: String!, $vendorId: String!) {
  customerReviews (storeId: $storeId, entityId: $vendorId, entityType: "Organization", filter:"status:APPROVED") {
    items {
      modifiedDate
      userName
      title
      review
      reviewStatus
    }
  }
}
```

